# Host-side configuration — copy to .env.host (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# These variables are read by scripts running on the HOST (cron-wrap.sh,
# run-docker.sh, task db:backup), never inside a container. Putting them in
# .env / .env.paper has NO effect: compose env_file only feeds containers.
# That mismatch is why the alert webhook was documented but never actually
# wired up, and why the system sat dead for two months (audit 0.3).
#
# cron-wrap.sh sources this file automatically. Nothing here is required —
# each var is a no-op when unset — but with all of it unset, a total outage
# is indistinguishable from a quiet market.

# --- Failure alerting -------------------------------------------------------
# JSON webhook (Slack / Discord / ntfy style). POSTed when a wrapped job exits
# nonzero. Tells you a job RAN AND FAILED.
# ALGO_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...

# --- Dead-man's switch ------------------------------------------------------
# healthchecks.io-style check URL. cron-wrap pings <URL>/start before the job,
# <URL> on success, <URL>/<exit-status> on failure. The monitor alerts when a
# ping does NOT arrive — the only mechanism that catches "the host is off" or
# "cron stopped firing", which is the failure mode that actually happened
# (host powered off 2026-07-22 through 2026-08-13, nothing noticed).
#
# Give each job its own check with its own expected schedule. A single shared
# URL means any one job pinging keeps a dead job looking green.
#
# Per-job override: ALGO_HEARTBEAT_URL_<LABEL>, where <LABEL> is the cron-wrap
# label uppercased with - replaced by _. Labels currently in the crontab:
#   paper-session, prod-session, weekly-learn, prod-backup, paper-backup
#
# ALGO_HEARTBEAT_URL=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
# ALGO_HEARTBEAT_URL_PAPER_SESSION=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
# ALGO_HEARTBEAT_URL_PROD_SESSION=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
# ALGO_HEARTBEAT_URL_WEEKLY_LEARN=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
# ALGO_HEARTBEAT_URL_PROD_BACKUP=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>
# ALGO_HEARTBEAT_URL_PAPER_BACKUP=https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>

# --- Backups ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Off-WSL copy target for `task db:backup` / `task paper:db:backup`. backups/
# alone lives in the same VHD as the volumes it backs up, so on its own it does
# not cover the risk it exists for. A Windows-side path works: /mnt/c/...
# ALGO_BACKUP_COPY_DIR=/mnt/c/Users/<you>/pinchy-backups
